---
/* The Salamon palace, Gračišće — a constructed illustration made for this
   archive by an image model from the brief at notes/image-prompts.md.
   The original is archived in the project's source library. */
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
---
<figure class="plate">
  <img src={u("/art/salamon-palace.webp")}
       alt="A constructed architectural elevation of the Salamon palace at Gračišće: a stone façade of three levels beside the outline of a fortified town gate; on the first floor a Venetian Gothic double-lancet window with a quatrefoil above and a balustraded balcony on carved corbels, flanked by two single ogee lancets; above them three round-arched windows under a band of dentil ornament; below, an arched doorway between barred openings."
       width="1269" height="1500" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
  <figcaption class="cap" style="margin-top:12px">
    <strong>The Salamon palace, Gračišće.</strong> A constructed illustration, made for this archive by an image model
    working from a written brief. It is illustration — it is not a survey, it is not measured, and nothing in it should
    be taken as a record of the building's real dimensions.
    <br /><br />
    What it follows is the published description: a two-storey building of carefully chiselled local stone standing
    beside the main gate, on which «architectural elements of the Gothic and Renaissance styles, popular in Venice in
    the late 15th century, exchange on the two storeys along the facade» — the floral Gothic double lancet and its
    balcony below, the simple semicircular arches and the row of classical decoration above. That alternation up the
    façade is the reason the building matters, and it is the one thing the picture gets right.
    <br /><br />
    The model returned it dressed as a conservation survey drawing, with a title block, a scale bar, dimension figures
    and a date. All of that was fabricated and all of it has been cropped away before publication, because a made-up
    measured drawing of a real protected building is a worse thing to put into the world than a plain picture. The
    number of ground-floor openings, the flanking lancets and every proportion in it are the model's invention. The
    unaltered original is in this project's source library, marked with what was removed.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .plate { margin: 0; }
  .plate img { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 560px; height: auto; border-radius: 2px; }
</style>
